{#
  _site_image_args.j2 — the SINGLE renderer for the site image build args.

  Every compose template whose service builds an image imports this macro
  rather than writing the loop itself, for the same reason `_network_axis.j2`
  and `_env_axis.j2` exist beside it: the axis is declared once for the whole
  stack, so a build arg added to the set has to reach every image OSPREY
  builds — not the subset whose templates someone remembered to edit.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  IMPORTING
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  The macro takes everything it needs as a parameter, so a plain (context-free)
  import is correct — never `with context`:

    Service templates, rendered by an Environment rooted at the PROJECT root
    (deployment/compose_generator.py's `FileSystemLoader(".")`, template paths
    like `services/<name>/docker-compose.yml.j2`):

      {% import "services/_site_image_args.j2" as site %}

    Templates rendered by an Environment rooted at this directory import by
    bare name instead:

      {% import "_site_image_args.j2" as site %}

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE `args` ARGUMENT
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  The mapping `compose_generator._stage_site_image_args_for_context` resolved
  for THIS service's build context — a CA for a TLS-intercepting proxy, pip's
  proxy bypass list, an internal package index — as the deployment's `images:`
  block declares them. The CA arrives already rewritten to the name staged
  INSIDE the context, because `COPY` cannot reach outside one. A deployment
  that declares none of them passes an empty mapping and nothing is emitted,
  so its build argv is what it always was.

  Rendered at BUILD time off the config rather than as a `${VAR}` default at
  compose time, for the reason the qmd fragment's own render-time gate states.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHITESPACE CONTRACT
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  As in `_network_axis.j2` and `_env_axis.j2`: the macro emits a LEADING
  newline and no trailing one, and is called alone on its own line with a
  left-trim marker, after the fixed entries of a build block's `args:`:

      {{- site.build_args(site_image_build_args | default({})) }}

  With nothing declared the macro emits the empty string and the whole line
  disappears, leaving the block byte-for-byte what it was — rather than the
  blank line an `{% if %}`/`{% endif %}` pair would have left.

  Mind the `{{-`: it strips ALL preceding whitespace, so do not place a call
  where a deliberate blank line precedes it.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHAT AN EDIT HERE REDDENS
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Every template that imports this file renders its macros, and those renders
  are pinned byte for byte. An edit to a macro below therefore moves the
  goldens of every importer at once — a wider reach than an edit to any one
  template, and one no importer can see from where it sits. Regenerate in the
  same change. One command per suite that pins an importer of this file:

      PYTHONPATH=src ./.venv/bin/python tests/templates/test_render_defaults_golden.py
      PYTHONPATH=src ./.venv/bin/python tests/templates/test_render_axis_shapes.py
      PYTHONPATH=src ./.venv/bin/python tests/deployment/test_lane_compose.py
      PYTHONPATH=src ./.venv/bin/python tests/deployment/test_va_compose_instances.py
#}

{#- The declared build args, one `NAME: "VALUE"` line each, sorted by name.

    `indent` defaults to the eight spaces an `args:` entry sits at in these
    templates, which is the only place this macro is called from. Sorted
    rather than author-ordered: the mapping is assembled by the resolver and
    never written by hand, so sorting is what makes a render a function of
    its context alone.

    A value is emitted as a quoted scalar a YAML parser reads back character
    for character, so no value a deployment can declare — a proxy URL carrying
    credentials among them — can end the scalar early and break the document
    around it. -#}
{%- macro build_args(args, indent=8) -%}
{%- set declared = args | default({}, true) -%}
{%- set entries = declared if declared is mapping else {} -%}
{%- set ns = namespace(lines=['']) -%}
{%- for name, value in entries | dictsort -%}
{%- set _ = ns.lines.append(' ' * indent ~ name ~ ': ' ~ (value | string | tojson)) -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if ns.lines | length > 1 -%}
{{ ns.lines | join('\n') }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
